{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfV1aqMkFE42B5QrezXu8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The task is complete. I investigated the `ft-2026.09` regression using the lab's decontamination and canary tools (19 of 20 re-run budget spent):\n\n**Evidence gathered:**\n- Decontamination sweeps across the 8 knob-value corners showed offline-decontam scores mostly track `capacity`/`mixture` restoration together, with `lr_scale` having comparatively little offline effect — the leak/contamination alone explained a good chunk of the offline-online gap but not all of it.\n- Key canary counterfactuals (the ones that actually settle causality):\n  - **Reset only `lr_scale`** to 1.198 (capacity, mixture held at release) → online = **0.733**, i.e. *no recovery* (even slightly worse than the shipped 0.7417). This rules out `lr_scale` as the cause.\n  - **Reset only `mixture`** to 0.760 (capacity, lr_scale held at release) → online = **0.7915**, a large recovery from the shipped 0.7417 toward the pre-release 0.8667. This isolates `mixture` as the lever that actually moves online quality.\n- This lines up with the training-team notes: lr_scale has \"always worked\" post model-size changes (unrelated to this incident), while the watched slice's small mixture share \"moves easily\" — consistent with it being starved by the new data source, which is invisible offline because the offline eval doesn't reflect real mixture-driven serving degradation.\n\n**Conclusion:** cause = `mixture`.\n\n**Fix written to `/app/report.json`:**\n```json\n{\n  \"cause\": \"mixture\",\n  \"fix\": {\n    \"capacity\": 0.759,\n    \"mixture\": 0.760,\n    \"lr_scale\": 1.198\n  }\n}\n```\nAll three knobs are restored to the farthest point the release constraints allow (their listed \"may be restored only as far as\" ceilings), since the decontaminated-offline sweep showed this combination gives the best recoverable offline score (0.8051) and doesn't require exceeding any cap. Budget remaining: 1 re-run (insufficient for another canary, which costs 4), so no further live verification was attempted — the two decisive canary counterfactuals above already satisfy the cause/fix logic needed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":68,"cache_read_input_tokens":33815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":68},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d56cd85b-9af6-45d5-90b1-99f4baf5c525","uuid":"25682e18-753f-4d4e-bbd6-56a200e96865","timestamp":"2026-09-28T02:00:27.037Z"}
